    {
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "These four documents show Washington naming corruption to the governments it was aiding and asking for administrative and fiscal change in return. The thread runs from the 1950 survey mission to Manila, through a 1961 conversation about President Garcia, to a 1978 aid proposal for Haiti that two departing officers thought would fail. They are here because each records what Americans said to the client or proposed to do about it, not only that they thought the government corrupt."
